/**
 * Checks whether the passed value is of type @see ctorValue.
 * If @see ctorValue is not passed, will allow for any basic value type (string, number, boolean).
 * In both cases, @see allowsEmpty can be used to either allow or forbid undefined/null values.
 * @param value the value to check the type of
 * @param ctorValue the optional prototype value should support
 * @param allowsEmpty if true, undefined or null is an allowed value, otherwise not.
 * @returns true if the type check succeeded, otherwise false
 */
